Does anyone else think that there are just too many charges in wands of 
wishing? I think the game would be improved quite a bit by lowering the 
maximum amount of wishes attainable to 3 (or so) instead of the current 
7. I have read a few YAAP's (and YAFAP's) that talk about the game being 
really easy after getting an early wand of wishing or the castle wand. 
Getting a single wish is about as unbalancing as finding the most 
unbalancing item (whatever that is), since you can wish for pretty much 
any item. Getting seven at once is just silly. You trudge all the way up 
Sokoban for an amulet of reflection or bag of holding and down the mines 
for a luckstone, but can just stumble upon something that can give all 
three plus GDSM, speed boots, GoP and an "oLS. This just seems broken. 
It just isn't fun in the long term to have such a crazily powerful 
reward.

Thus, I propose either making a wand of wishing unrechargable (giving a 
maximum of 4 wishes) or giving it a maximum of 1 charge (giving a 
maximum of 3 wishes).

I would also be quite happy if both the above were done, giving a 
maximum of 2 wishes.

What do people think? (and why?)

